This document provides AI agents with the necessary knowledge and rules for understanding and editing this document repository.

## Directory Structure

- **Root Directory**: Contains daily work documents.
- **`docs/`**: Contains final output documents that may be synced online.
- **`prompts/`**: Contains prompts and workflow definitions for agents.

## File Naming Convention

- Standard documents: `YYYY-MM-DD-hh 分类 - 标题.md`
- Daily summaries: `YYYY-MM-DD-hh 📅 摘要.md`
- Weekly summaries: `YYYY-MM-DD-hh 📅 本周摘要 YYYY-MM-DD - YYYY-MM-DD.md`

## Special Symbol Definition

- `🟥`: Represents a TODO, an unfinished item, a shelved/postponed item, or information that needs to be added.
- `🟩`: Represents a DONE item or completed information.
- `🟨`: Represents an item in progress.
- `❇️`: Represents work reflected only in code/Agent sessions (Gemini-cli / Antigravity), not in Obsidian notes.
- `💡`: Represents a new idea.
- `📅️`: Represents a periodic summary.

## Workflows

This section defines abstract workflows.

### Weekly Summary Workflow

#### When to call
At the end of the work week.

#### Input
- The previous weekly summary document.
- All documents created between the last summary and today.
- A project background document.

#### Process
1.  Read all input documents.
2.  Synthesize the progress on ongoing projects from the last summary.
3.  Identify newly completed tasks, new ongoing tasks, and new ideas from the new documents.
4.  Structure the new summary following the standard template.
5.  Pay special attention to items marked with `🟥` (TODOs).

#### Output Document
- **Title**: `{YYYY-MM-DD-hh} 📅 本周摘要 {YYYY-MM-DD} - {YYYY-MM-DD}.md`
- **Content**: A summary of the week's progress, structured according to the template.
